From 8c5a28f80ccd8275abd9cfce7f12a6c50b854e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:54:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: set drvdata before
 registering clocks

The prepare and vote callbacks of the q6dsp clocks take the q6dsp_cc
from the driver data of the clock controller, but q6dsp_clock_dev_probe()
sets it only after it has registered every clock. Registering a clock
adopts the orphan clocks whose parent it is, and recalculating their
rate can runtime-resume the device that provides them, which prepares
the new clock before the probe has finished.

That happens when the ADSP of a QCS6490 board is stopped and started:
the WSA macro clocks are orphans by then, and the prepare reads desc
from a NULL q6dsp_cc (offset 0x348):

  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1]  SMP
  Workqueue: pdr_notifier_wq pdr_notifier_work
  pc : clk_q6dsp_prepare+0x24/0x40
  Call trace:
   clk_q6dsp_prepare+0x24/0x40 (P)
   clk_core_prepare+0x5c/0x160
   clk_prepare+0x28/0x44
   pm_clk_resume+0x10c/0x188
   wsa_macro_runtime_resume+0x2c/0x48
   ...
   clk_core_reparent_orphans_nolock+0xa0/0xd0
   __clk_register+0x5d0/0xa20
   devm_clk_hw_register+0x5c/0xe0
   q6dsp_clock_dev_probe+0x118/0x1e0

Set the driver data before the first clock is registered.

Fixes: 9ab71ac37240 ("ASoC: qdsp6: q6afe-clocks: move audio-clocks to common file")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c | 9 ++-------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
index 03838582aead..69e5548ee35d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	cc->desc = desc;
 	cc->dev = dev;
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
@@ -174,12 +175,6 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider(dev, q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get, cc);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
-	return 0;
+	return devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider(dev, q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get, cc);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
